== Notes ==

*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
* The slaying is done with [[divine damage]] equal to the target's current [[hit point]]s. (Thus divine [[damage resistance]] or [[immunity]] &ndash; rare in general, and more so for undead creatures &ndash; could save a target.)
* This spell goes through walls, so it can inadvertently kill undead not yet seen by the caster.
* The number of hit dice affected is actually a single roll of a d4, which is then multiplied by the caster level.
* The maximized version of this spell is bugged in that it does not cap caster level, allowing a level 40 caster to slay 160 hit dice of undead. (The normal version can affect at most 80 hit dice.)
*The spell description incorrectly states that it affects the closest undead first; the most distant undead creature in the area of effect is affected first ''(possibly a bug)''.
* The type of save for this spell (will) happens to be the high save for the [[monster class|undead class]], which is possessed by many of the undead [[race]]. This can make the [[difficulty class|DC]] an important consideration.

